{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_13bc05a07d17:reviewer:commit:1:0","created_at":"2026-09-17 14:06:53","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"agent","role":"reviewer","provider":"claude-code"}},"payload":{"step_name":"reviewer:commit","phase":"1","iteration":0,"result_json":{"readiness":"ready_with_corrections","items":[{"id":"P1.1","title":"Exclude polish findings from P and the single-item architecture alert","action":"auto_fix","reason":"deriveBudget passes unfiltered findings to computeGrossP and the singleArchitectureReviewPoints scan. Plan defines pending as scopeClass !== polish and names the parameter pendingFindings. A polish finding with architectureDelta 5 currently raises positive_architecture_exceeded and requiresHuman. Filter polish once in deriveBudget and add a test.","priority":"P1"},{"id":"P1.2","title":"Drop the DCn regex from isCompleteDebtClaimEvidence","action":"auto_fix","reason":"The guard is also applied to reviewer creditClaim, whose id format the plan does not constrain and which must not collide with author DCn. A complete intrinsic reviewer claim with id RC1 silently yields N = 0. Plan bullet requires only presence of debtClaimId; the Phase 2 parser enforces DCn format. Require a non-empty string id and add a non-DC reviewer-claim test.","priority":"P1"},{"id":"P1.3","title":"Stop fabricating thresholds.mode = advisory in deriveBudget","action":"auto_fix","reason":"Input config omits mode but DerivedBudgetResult.thresholds is the full config, so the code hardcodes advisory and misreports enforced projects. Follow the plan configSnapshot precedent: type thresholds as Omit<ReviewBudgetConfig, \"mode\">, return input.config, remove the unused defaults import, and update the plan 1.1 type block.","priority":"P1"},{"id":"P2.1","title":"Remove the tautological still-listed branch in computePendingR","action":"auto_fix","reason":"stillListedIds is built from the iterated findings, so the check is always true and incorporatedIds never affects the result. Output is correct per the plan R definition; collapse to a non-polish sum and comment why the parameter does not change the total.","priority":"P2"},{"id":"P2.2","title":"Add missing band and requiresHuman test coverage","action":"auto_fix","reason":"Plan test matrix lists bands and requiresHuman flags but only over_effective is asserted. Add within_standard, within_debt_allowance, over_absolute, semanticHumanRequired alone, I null, and P equal to the limit.","priority":"P2"},{"id":"P2.3","title":"Freeze DEFAULT_REVIEW_BUDGET_CONFIG","action":"auto_fix","reason":"The shared defaults object is mutable; freeze it so callers cannot alter defaults used by every derivation.","priority":"P2"}],"summary":"Phase 1 types and pure arithmetic match the plan formulas and pass tests, typecheck, and lint. Three mechanical contract fixes are needed before later phases consume them: polish findings leak into P and requiresHuman, the DCn regex silently zeroes reviewer-introduced credit claims, and deriveBudget hardcodes thresholds.mode."},"head_commit":"825686db4d5092dfe435a6c4982d86f3eff05127","patch_id":null,"diff_summary":{"files_changed":0,"insertions":0,"deletions":0},"duration_ms":153201,"tokens_in":34,"tokens_out":12515,"cost_usd":2.7324732500000004,"model":"fable"}}
